Plan 9 animated-emission benchmark
===================================

Command:
  cmake --build /tmp/blackhole-renderer-plan9-headless --target animated-emission-benchmark --parallel 4
  /tmp/blackhole-renderer-plan9-headless/app/animated-emission-benchmark

The benchmark uses CUDA events, two warmups and ten measured frames at 1920x1080,
with the accepted Plan 8 bloom-on appearance and no starfield sampling. Static and
animated paths use the same persistent output/workspace shape.

Observed RTX 3080 / CUDA 12.0.140 results:
  run 0: static_gpu_ms=172.0329 animated_gpu_ms=166.6625 overhead_ms=-5.3705 overhead_percent=-3.122
  run 1: static_gpu_ms=466.2015 animated_gpu_ms=451.6690 overhead_ms=-14.5325 overhead_percent=-3.117
  run 2: static_gpu_ms=462.4650 animated_gpu_ms=444.3565 overhead_ms=-18.1086 overhead_percent=-3.916
  run 3: static_gpu_ms=464.0268 animated_gpu_ms=444.2744 overhead_ms=-19.7524 overhead_percent=-4.257

The first run is a warm GPU/cache state; subsequent runs show variable system load.
Animated emission adds no measurable GPU cost in this benchmark. These results are
render cost measurements, not a 60 FPS playback claim.
